303 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 153 0 R
/E (My name is Pauline Silk, and I'm delighted to introduce myself as the new Editor of the Leeds and Broomfield Church and Village News.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
304 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 153 0 R
/E (Firstly, I'd like to say a heartfelt thank you to Judi Taylor for her incredible dedication over the past 27 years. Producing a community magazine month after month is no small task, and I hope I can continue the wonderful work she has done in keeping our churches, villages and community connected.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
305 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 153 0 R
/E (A little about me... I grew up in the neighbouring village of Otham and now live in Langley, so village life has always been a big part of who I am. I love being involved in the local community and have been fortunate to help organise and support a number of local events over the years.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
306 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 153 0 R
/E (I feel incredibly honoured to have been given the opportunity to take on this role and hope I can do Judi proud. My aim is to build on the strong foundations she has created while introducing a few fresh ideas along the way.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
307 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 153 0 R
/E (I hope this magazine continues to be at the heart of our churches and villages - keeping everyone informed, celebrating the people, organisations and events that make our community so special, and helping neighbours stay connected.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
308 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 153 0 R
/E (I'd love this magazine to reflect all aspects of life across our churches and villages, so if you have a story to share, an event to promote, news from your organisation, or photographs from community activities, I'd be delighted to hear from you.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
309 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 153 0 R
/E (Thank you for the warm welcome I've already received. I look forward to getting to know even more of you through these pages and hope you'll enjoy reading each edition as much as I'll enjoy putting it together.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
310 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
