338 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 155 0 R
/E (I wonder what is your most memorable event, maybe surviving the summer heat, getting married, buying a house or enjoying a wonderful holiday. Mine certainly includes all of these but I can now add being ordained. Yes, even in my retirement! Permit me to explain. On Saturday 4th July at Canterbury Cathedral, along with twelve others, I was ordained as Deacon to serve as an Assistant Curate.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
339 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 155 0 R
/E ( A Deacon is someone who serves God, the Church and the Community which includes bringing to the Church the needs and hopes of all the people. My area of service is the Castle Churches Benefice which includes Otham, Langley, Leeds, Broomfield and Kingswood. )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
