500 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 164 0 R
/E (What an extraordinary summer it has been. After complaining about seemingly endless rain earlier in the year, we have certainly experienced the other extreme over recent months, with prolonged periods of very hot and dry weather. The drought has presented its own challenges across the Estate, particularly for our Gardens and Grounds teams, who have worked incredibly hard to care for the gardens and wider landscape through some very difficult conditions. I suspect many of you have been facing similar challenges in your own gardens!)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
501 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 164 0 R
/E (Despite the heat, it has been a very busy summer at Leeds Castle. Families have spent the school holidays exploring our Little People, BIG DREAMS trail, discovering the stories of 12 extraordinary women from Marie Curie and Agatha Christie to Mary Earps and Emmeline Pankhurst. It has been lovely to see children engaging with their stories and, hopefully, leaving the Estate with a few big dreams of their own.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
502 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 164 0 R
/E (We also welcomed thousands of motoring enthusiasts for Motors by the Moat in August, with hundreds of vehicles on display across the Estate alongside live entertainment and driving displays. It is always a very different weekend at Leeds Castle and wonderful to see such a diverse collection of vehicles against the rather unusual backdrop of a 900-year old Castle.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
503 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 165 0 R
/E (15)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
504 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 165 0 R
/T (As the school summer holidays come to an end, our annual Sculpture Trail has returned to the Estate and will run throughout September. Sculptures created by a range of talented artists have been positioned around the gardens and grounds, creating some unexpected encounters as you explore. One of the pleasures of the trail is seeing contemporary art sitting within this historic landscape, and perhaps discovering corners of the Estate you might otherwise walk straight past.)
/E (As the school summer holidays come to an end, our annual Sculpture Trail has returned to the Estate and will run throughout September. Sculptures created by a range of talented artists have been positioned around the gardens and grounds, creating some unexpected encounters as you explore. One of the pleasures of the trail is seeing contemporary art sitting within this historic landscape, and perhaps discovering corners of the Estate you might otherwise walk straight past.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
505 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 165 0 R
/T (September may only just mark the beginning of autumn, but behind the scenes our thoughts are already turning towards Christmas. We were delighted, earlier this summer, to announce that Wallace & Gromit will be coming to Leeds Castle for Christmas 2026.)
/E (September may only just mark the beginning of autumn, but behind the scenes our thoughts are already turning towards Christmas. We were delighted, earlier this summer, to announce that Wallace & Gromit will be coming to Leeds Castle for Christmas 2026.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
506 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 165 0 R
/T (The Castle will be transformed for a brand-new festive experience featuring the much loved Aardman characters, and preparations are already well underway to bring everything to life ahead of opening in November. We are tremendously excited about the partnership and look forward to sharing much more over the coming months.)
/E (The Castle will be transformed for a brand-new festive experience featuring the much loved Aardman characters, and preparations are already well underway to bring everything to life ahead of opening in November. We are tremendously excited about the partnership and look forward to sharing much more over the coming months.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [3]
>>
